From 1156ba3e3bdc2ffd2d808b1e66b4deaaffa2bf71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 15:39:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 207/212] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-google: Add rear camera VCM

The rear IMX363 module on blueline and crosshatch carries an Onsemi
LC898219XI voice coil motor on CCI master 0. The downstream firmware
update code addresses it at write address 0xE4 (7-bit 0x72) and checks
register 0xF0 for the 0xA5 chip ID, matching the lc89821x driver.

The LC898219XI is a single supply part: its only rail, VDD, feeds the
logic, the hall sensor and the OUT1/OUT2 coil driver. On this board that
rail is CAM_VANA0, the GPIO16-switched 2.8 V supply the sensor already
uses as vana. Downstream talks to the VCM right after the sensor power-up
with no actuator rail enabled, and on hardware the chip only acknowledges
and tracks focus targets once that rail is up, so share the regulator.
Link the lens to the sensor with lens-focus so the subdev notifier binds
them.

The VCM driver talks on CCI0 as soon as the lens subdev is opened, which
can happen before the sensor is powered. The IMX363 I/O pads and the
VD6281 colour sensor on the same bus are fed from LVS1 and clamp SDA/SCL
when it is off, so keep LVS1 always on for now.

The module also has an LC898123F40 OIS controller at 0x3e and the VCM
EEPROM at 0x73; neither has a mainline driver, so only note them.

Signed-off-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-google-common.dtsi     | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-google-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-google-common.dtsi
index 552293955eca..ef6d23d39c72 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-google-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-google-common.dtsi
@@ -387,6 +387,12 @@ vreg_l28a_3p0: ldo28 {
 		vreg_lvs1_1p8: lvs1 {
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			/*
+			 * Camera I/O rail. The IMX363 and the VD6281 colour sensor
+			 * share CCI0 with the VCM and clamp the bus when this rail
+			 * is off, so keep it on until the bus users are sequenced.
+			 */
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 	};
 
@@ -503,6 +509,8 @@ rear_cam: camera@1a {
 		rotation = <90>;
 		orientation = <MEDIA_ORIENTATION_BACK>;
 
+		lens-focus = <&rear_cam_vcm>;
+
 		port {
 			cam_rear_endpoint: endpoint {
 				data-lanes = <1 2 3 4>;
@@ -511,6 +519,15 @@ cam_rear_endpoint: endpoint {
 			};
 		};
 	};
+
+	/* OIS controller (Onsemi LC898123F40) @3e, VCM EEPROM @73 */
+
+	rear_cam_vcm: camera-lens@72 {
+		compatible = "onnn,lc898219xi";
+		reg = <0x72>;
+
+		vdd-supply = <&camera_rear_avdd>;
+	};
 };
 
 &cci_i2c1 {
